      <div type="clause" n="16">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Af">Af</ref> 16</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="16" corresp="#wit-e"><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#Af_16.lnote.oe.13"/><pb n="58" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif mon cu oððe stodmyran<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#Af_16.lnote.oe.14"/> forstele<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#Af_16.lnote.oe.15"/> ⁊ folan oððe cealf ófadrife<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#Af_16.lnote.oe.16"/>, forgelde<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#Af_16.lnote.oe.17"/> mid<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="**" target="#Af_16.lnote.oe.star2"/> scill. ⁊ þa moder<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#Af_16.lnote.oe.18"/> be hiora<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#Af_16.lnote.oe.19"/> weorðe.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#Af_16.lnote.oe.20"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="16" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="58" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif mon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_16.lnote.oe.1"/> cú oþþe stodmyran<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_16.lnote.oe.2"/> forstele ⁊ folan oððe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_16.lnote.oe.5"/> cealf ofadrifeð, forgilde mid scyllinge ⁊ ða modor<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Af_16.lnote.oe.6"/> be heora<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Af_16.lnote.oe.7"/> weorðe.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Af_16.lnote.oe.7"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="16" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="58" ed="#liebermann"/>Be<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_16.lnote.oe.1-2"/> ða<hi rend="italic">m</hi> gif man of myran folan adrifþ oððe cucealf. Gyf man cu oððe stodmære forstele ⁊ folan oððe cealf ofadrife, forgylde mid sixtig<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_16.lnote.oe.2-2"/> scill' ⁊ þa modor be heora wyrðe.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="16" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="59" ed="#liebermann"/>Si quis uaccam uel equam uel<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#Af_16.lnote.oe.11"/> pullum uel uitulum furetur uel abducat<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#Af_16.lnote.oe.12"/> (pregnantes affligat), reddat<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#Af_16.lnote.oe.13-2"/> partum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#Af_16.lnote.oe.14-2"/> solido uno et matrem secundum pretium estimatum.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="72" ed="#attenborough"/>[Be ðam gif man of myran folan adrifþ oððe cucealf.] Gif mon cu oððe stodmyran<ptr type="editorNote" n="4" target="#Af_16.attnote.fn.4"/> forstele ⁊ folan oððe cealf ófadrife<ptr type="editorNote" n="5" target="#Af_16.attnote.fn.5"/>, forgelde mid scill.<ptr type="editorNote" n="6" target="#Af_16.attnote.fn.6"/> ⁊ þa moder be hiora weorðe.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="18" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="310" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>Gif mon cu oððe stodmyran forstele ⁊ folan oððe cealf ófadrife, forgelde mid scill ⁊ þa moder be hiora weorðe.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="59" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_16.lnote.de.1"/> jemand eine Kuh oder Mutterstute<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_16.lnote.de.2"/> stiehlt und Fohlen oder Kalb forttreibt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_16.lnote.de.3"/>, ersetze er [letzteres dem Bestohlenen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_16.lnote.de.4"/>] mit [1] Schilling<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_16.lnote.de.5"/> und die Mutter[thiere]<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Af_16.lnote.de.6"/> je nach ihrem Werthe.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Af_16.lnote.de.7"/></ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If someone steals a cow or a brood-mare and drives off the foal or calf, let him repay [the latter to the one robbed] with [1] shilling and the mother [animals] according to their value.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="73" ed="#attenborough"/>If anyone steals a cow or a broodmare, and drives off a foal or a calf, he shall pay for the latter a shilling, and for the mothers according to their value.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="412" ed="#whitelock"/>If anyone steals a cow or a brood-mare and drives off a foal or a calf, he is to pay a shilling compensation [for the latter], and for the mothers according to their value.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="311" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>If a person steals a cow or stud-mare and drives away a foal or calf, let him compensate with a shilling and for the mothers according to their worth.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="282"><label>possibly derived from</label> <ref target="clause:Af_El-to-24">Af El 24</ref> <quote>Af 16 (if not Af Int 24)</quote></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_16.lnote.oe.13" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">58</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Capiteltrennung nach B’s Rubricator Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">chapter division in Ld following B’s rubricator</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_16.lnote.oe.14" n="14" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">58</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="spaced">myre</hi> <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">myre</hi> Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_16.lnote.oe.15" n="15" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">58</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-stæle <hi rend="italic">So</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-stæle So</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_16.lnote.oe.16" n="16" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">58</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-dryfe <hi rend="italic">So</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-dryfe So</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_16.lnote.oe.17" n="17" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">58</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-gyld <hi rend="italic">So;</hi> -gylde <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-gyld So; -gylde Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_16.lnote.oe.star2" n="**" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">58</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">þam … [<hi rend="italic">Lücke für 1 Wort</hi>] mid anum scill' <hi rend="italic">So;</hi> feowrtigum <hi rend="italic">fügt zu Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">þam … [gap for 1 word] mid anum scill' So; feowrtigum added by Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_16.lnote.oe.18" n="18" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">58</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">modor <hi rend="italic">So Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">modor So Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_16.lnote.oe.19" n="19" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">58</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">heora <hi rend="italic">So Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">heora So Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_16.lnote.oe.20" n="20" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">58</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">wyrþe <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">wyrþe Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_16.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">58</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">o <hi rend="italic">geändert in</hi> a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">o altered to a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_16.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">58</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">y <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">y on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_16.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">58</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">übergeschr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">written above</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_16.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">58</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> moder</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">altered to moder</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_16.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">58</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">e <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">e on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_16.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">59</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">u. p. u. u. <hi rend="italic">übergeschr. Co, im Texte Or, fehlt übrigen</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">u. p. u. u. written above in Co, in the text in Or, lacking in the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_16.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">59</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">nur</hi> ab. <hi rend="italic">Lond; nur</hi> pr. af. <hi rend="italic">übrige</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">only ab. Lond; only pr. af. the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_16.lnote.oe.13-2" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">59</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">reducat <hi rend="italic">st.</hi> reddat p. <hi rend="italic">K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">reducat instead of reddat p. K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_16.lnote.oe.14-2" n="14" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">59</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">pro <hi rend="italic">fügt zu Hk Brti</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">pro added by Hk Brti</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_16.lnote.oe.1-2" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">58</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Rubrik am unteren Rande</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">rubric in the lower margin</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_16.lnote.oe.2-2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">58</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">unterstrichen, darüber im</hi> 16. <hi rend="italic">Jh.</hi> feowertigum</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">underlined, with feowertigum written above it in the 16th cent.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_16.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">54</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘Davon, wenn jemand von der Stute das Fohlen oder ein Kuhkalb forttreibt’ Rb B; nicht ‘drives off a mare’s foal’, weil das <hi rend="italic">of</hi> vor Objekt nicht Adverb sein kann; Thorpe versetzte <hi rend="italic">of</hi> vor <hi rend="italic">adrifð. Cucealf</hi> als Kompositum belegt Toller <hi rend="italic">Suppl.</hi> auch sonst, hält trotzdem <hi rend="italic">cu</hi> möglicherweise für gen. In verwandten Sprachen heisst ‘Kalb’ auch das Junge anderer Tiere als der Kuh; Kluge <hi rend="italic">Etym. Wb.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘Of someone driving off the foal from the mare, or a cow-calf’ Rb B; not ‘drives off a mare’s foal’, because the <hi rend="italic">of</hi> before an object cannot be an adverb; Thorpe moved <hi rend="italic">of</hi> to before <hi rend="italic">adrifð. Cucealf</hi> as a compound is attested elsewhere too by Toller <hi rend="italic">Suppl.</hi>, who nevertheless considers <hi rend="italic">cu</hi> possibly a gen. In related languages ‘calf’ also denotes the young of animals other than the cow; Kluge <hi rend="italic">Etym. Wb.</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_16.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">54</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Gestütsmähre; <hi rend="italic">vgl.</hi> 9, 2</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Stud mare; <hi rend="italic">cf.</hi> 9, 2</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_16.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">54</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Toller 729a trennt besser <hi rend="italic">of adrife.</hi> — Q <hi rend="smallcaps">ii</hi> missversteht Abtreiben der Frucht (daher <hi rend="italic">pullum uel uitulum</hi> streichend), wohl infolge Zweideutigkeit des Lateinischen <hi rend="italic">abigere</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Toller 729a better divides <hi rend="italic">of adrife.</hi> — Q <hi rend="smallcaps">ii</hi> misunderstands this as causing a miscarriage (hence deleting <hi rend="italic">pullum uel uitulum</hi>), probably owing to the ambiguity of the Latin <hi rend="italic">abigere</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_16.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">54</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Dazu Diebstahlstrafe; Af 9, 2. — Hinter <hi rend="italic">þam</hi> las wohl So ein Wort für ‘Eigentümer’</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">In addition the penalty for theft; Af 9, 2. — After <hi rend="italic">þam</hi>, So probably read a word for ‘owner’</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_16.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">55</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Inst Cn setzen den Normann. Schilling. — So’s Zufügung ‘einem’ zeigt spätere Sprache. Ld’s ‘40’ ist unmöglich, da ein Ochs nur 30 Pfg. galt</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Inst Cn use the Norman shilling. — So’s addition ‘one’ shows later language. Ld’s ‘40’ is impossible, since an ox was worth only 30 pence</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_16.lnote.de.6" n="6" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">55</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">hiora</hi> ist Plural, also auch <hi rend="italic">moder</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">hiora</hi> is plural, hence so is <hi rend="italic">moder</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_16.lnote.de.7" n="7" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">55</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Taxe</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Taxe</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_16.attnote.fn.4" n="4" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">72</biblScope></bibl><label>stodmyran</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">stodmære</hi>. B.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_16.attnote.fn.5" n="5" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">72</biblScope></bibl><label>ófadrife</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">ofadrifeð</hi>. H.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_16.attnote.fn.6" n="6" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">72</biblScope></bibl><label>scill</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">sixtig</hi>. B. Underlined and <hi rend="italic">feowertigum</hi> written above it in 16th century. <hi rend="italic">feowrtigum</hi>. Ld.</seg></note>
